Sval: send only the primary language

A new RFPTarget, LanguagesPrimaryOnly, reduces the language list a site sees
to its first language and that language's base, so "de-CH, fr, en" reads as
["de-CH", "de"]: in navigator.languages for windows
(Navigator::GetLanguages) and workers (WorkerNavigator::GetLanguages), in
the Accept-Language header, and as the default locale of window, worker and
worklet realms, which then matches navigator.language. A DevTools or
WebDriver language override still wins. SvalRFPService::SpoofLanguages is
the one reduction all of them use.

It is Doc-gated, so granularOverrides lifts it per site. The header follows
the same decision: nsHttpChannel::AsyncOpen composes the channel check with
the load's granular overrides, as Document::ShouldResistFingerprinting
does, once AntiTrackingUtils::UpdateAntiTrackingInfoForChannel has put
them on the load info. It sets Accept-Language wherever the header is still
one of nsHttpHandler's two forms, so a redirect, which copies the header,
carries the final site's.

No chrome API can change what these report per site: intl.accept_languages
is one global pref.

